    },
    {
      "question": "Is the course beginner-friendly?",
      "answer": "Yes. Basic computer and design literacy is helpful, and a Photoshop/Canva orientation should be available."
    },
    {
      "question": "What software is primarily taught?",
      "answer": "Adobe Photoshop."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I use Canva?",
      "answer": "Canva is an accessible alternative for suitable design tasks, although advanced Photoshop compositing capabilities may differ."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is Photoshop included in the fee?",
      "answer": "Software licensing depends on Nova Skills' verified arrangements. Do not assume a personal license is included."
    },
    {
      "question": "Will I learn subject cutouts?",
      "answer": "Yes. Subject isolation, layer masks and edge refinement are included."
    },
    {
      "question": "Will I learn realistic compositing?",
      "answer": "Yes. The curriculum covers lighting, shadows, depth, colour harmonization and image correction."
    },
    {
      "question": "Will I learn typography?",
      "answer": "Yes. Students practise hierarchy, type selection, legibility and title-thumbnail alignment."
    },
    {
      "question": "How many thumbnails will I design?",
      "answer": "Twelve finished thumbnails."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the portfolio structure?",
      "answer": "Six original primary concepts and six meaningful variations across at least three content categories."
    },
    {
      "question": "What is a meaningful variation?",
      "answer": "An alternative creative direction with a clear hypothesis, such as a different focal point, composition or visual message—not just a small colour change."
    },
    {
      "question": "Will I learn mobile thumbnail design?",
      "answer": "Yes. Students review readability, hierarchy and composition at reduced display sizes."
    },
    {
      "question": "Will I learn YouTube thumbnail A/B testing?",
      "answer": "Yes. The course teaches eligible native YouTube title/thumbnail testing and how to interpret its results."
    },
    {
      "question": "Does YouTube support native thumbnail A/B testing for Shorts?",
      "answer": "No. Current native A/B testing does not support Shorts."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can Shorts have custom thumbnails?",
      "answer": "Current YouTube guidance separately permits custom Shorts thumbnail uploads through eligible desktop Studio workflows. This is not the same as native A/B testing."
    },
    {
      "question": "What determines the winner of YouTube's native A/B test?",
      "answer": "YouTube uses watch-time share rather than CTR alone."
    },
    {
      "question": "Must I have my own YouTube channel?",
      "answer": "No. Portfolio creation and simulated testing plans do not require a personal channel."
    },
    {
      "question": "Must I run a live A/B test?",
      "answer": "No. An evidence-based testing plan is acceptable when an eligible, authorized channel is unavailable."
    },
    {
      "question": "What if the A/B test has no clear winner?",
      "answer": "Tests may be inconclusive or show similar performance. Students learn to report those outcomes accurately."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can AI assist thumbnail design?",
      "answer": "AI may help with ideation and suitable design workflows, but human review, visual accuracy and applicable licensing remain essential."
    },
